			{
				"property": "",
				"friendlyName": "Start Cooking With Settings",
				"channel": "start_cook",
				"type": "String",
				"refresh": false,
				"actions": [
					{
						"command": "action",
						"parameterType": "JSON",
						"siid": 2,
						"aiid": 4
					}
				],
				"readmeComment": "Starts cooking with a JSON list of 8 values: time (minutes), temperature (degrees Celsius), recipe id, keep warm after cooking (true or false), scheduled start time (minutes, 0 starts now), cooking weight (grams), food quantity (1 single layer, 2 double layer), texture (0 none, 1 air fry, 2 steam and air fry, 3 steam). The recipe id is `M` plus the mode number (for example `M1` air fry custom, `M8` steam custom) or `C` plus the recipeID of a cloud recipe. The Mi Home app shows that cooking cannot be started from the app, so the device may refuse a remote start. Example air frying 15 minutes at 180 degrees: `[15,180,\"M1\",false,0,500,1,1]`. The texture values follow the Mi Home app, which uses the same list for st701o and st701t."
			},
